    "description": "Record the D4b R1 benchmark cases\n\nD4b revision R1: four benchmark cases from Martian and ReviewBench join the eval case set in jerridan/pr-review-cases PR #8. This PR records R1 in TICKETS.md, in the same shape as the R4 line.\n\n- Cases: `martian-sentry-67876` (Python, 297 changed lines), `martian-calcom-10600` (TypeScript, 316), `reviewbench-spm-19` (TypeScript, 543) and `reviewbench-node-postgres-3650` (JavaScript, 568). 56 goldens: 32 posted, 24 not real. The set holds 18 cases and 142 goldens.\n- The labeling loop set every severity (three runs per finding). No finding went to the human queue.\n- `reviewbench-42-transcendence-115` is built but not labeled: the usage limit of the judge stopped its labels two times. A later revision can add it.\n- No pin move, no baseline and no version bump. The final D4b baseline PR moves the pin one time for the four revisions (TICKETS.md, D4b). The change touches no shipped file.\n- Merge order: pr-review-cases PR #8 first, then this PR.\n\nChecks: `npm test` (1382 passed), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZgpJZ1ahheDxuskhj2\n",
